WEBVTT

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.130
Rika!

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:37.140
It ended in tragedy again...

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:46.980
A thousand years ago...

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.950
When I was despairing over the
cruel nature of the world of men,

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:52.530
I took on the sins of the world

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:57.870
and cleansed the men to whom
I offered myself in sacrifice.

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:01.710
The one I entrusted with that sacrifice

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:04.080
was my very own daughter.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.170
In the millennia that passed afterwards,

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:09.800
I continued to despise the world of man.

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:13.760
But nothing lasts forever.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:19.310
Not walls, not doors, not hearts.

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:24.230
Not even the power that kept me
sealed away from the human world.

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:29.480
Furude family lore declares that,
if for eight consecutive generations,

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:33.700
the first-born Furude child is a girl,
then Oyashiro-<i>sama </i>will be reincarnated.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:39.120
That's why, Rika, when you were born
as the eighth consecutive female child...

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:40.790
At long last--

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:46.080
I finally had regained
my view of the human world.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:51.840
The millennia I spent
rejecting the world of men

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:55.180
was no more than a
cage of my own loneliness.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:58.140
Perhaps that one-sided
despair was punishment

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:04.190
for forcing my daughter
to carry out that horrific act.

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:14.610
When girls continued to be born into
the family and your mother was with child,

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:19.530
oh, how I prayed it would be a girl.

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:23.330
You would be my first friend in a
thousand years, my very own daughter,

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:27.040
with whom I would share life.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:31.800
But in that first June of 1983,

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:36.050
I committed a grave sin once more.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.560
To avert your fated death,

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.430
I granted you power and turned
you into one who lives in loops.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:48.650
Goodnight, now,

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:50.570
Rika-<i>chan</i>.

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:01.410
But my power was imperfect.

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:06.210
It would only bring you
a hundred years of suffering.

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:09.830
Your spirit was driven
to the brink of death,

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:15.510
and you cursed the dice of fate that
continued to bequeath despair unto you.

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:18.340
And yet...

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:20.300
...you never gave up.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:27.350
I'm Hanyuu Furude.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:34.360
She's so cute! Wait, Furude?

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:37.820
That's right!
She's a distant relative of mine!

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:44.740
Your strength changed my role
from mere bystander to participant.

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:47.460
Then...

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.830
The human world is
just like a game of Old Maid.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.630
I happened to draw the Joker.

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:55.550
But there's nobody else
to pass the card to now.

00:03:55.550 --> 00:03:58.840
So in revenge, I'm going to shoot you all!

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:01.890
Fitting for this irrational
world of men, isn't it?!

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:06.220
Hanyuu?!

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:10.400
Brave Mion. You've shown
more than enough courage.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:15.650
If the Joker can't be passed
to anyone else in this world of men,

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:19.240
then it is my job to accept it.

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:22.120
Hanyuu, what are you doing?!

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:26.330
Rika, I had so much fun in this world.

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:30.370
It was so much more fun to play
with you in club than to just watch.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.920
Thank you.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:36.170
Spending time with you all brought me
more happiness than a god could handle.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:39.630
Come, shoot me, child of man,

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:43.720
with that sin you must foist
onto another in this world of men!

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:48.180
Fine. Fine, fine, <i>fine</i>!

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:50.190
Then die!

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:57.530
After witnessing a miracle
in the world of men,

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:02.490
I, Hanyuu, returned
to the sea of fragments.

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:05.330
Good night, Rika.

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:07.040
Sweet dreams.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:37.400
Rika...

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:43.110
Despite what it meant,
I was so happy to see you again.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:13.950
HIGURASHI: WHEN THEY CRY SOTSU

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.750
You little brat!

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:22.170
Talk! Talk!

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:27.630
Talk! Talk! Talk!

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:33.520
Everything is okay now, Rika.

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:38.400
That pain is no more than a memory.

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:42.110
You should not be able to feel it now.

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:46.400
Ooishi killed me!

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:53.740
Huh? I remember who killed me.

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:55.540
What's going on?

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:01.330
What foolishness.

00:08:03.630 --> 00:08:09.720
If only you'd stayed with the cat until
the end. You might have helped her.

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:11.850
If she remembers who killed her,

00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:17.020
then won't that make
our methods even more effective?

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:21.100
A hundred years! A century I was trapped
in Hinamizawa, like a bird in a cage!

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:24.770
I witnessed tragedy after tragedy
without knowing the reason <i>why</i>!

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:29.450
If it wasn't for my friends and their
miracle, my soul would be long dead!

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:32.700
To my mind, time has long passed 1983!

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:36.040
I'm not this little girl anymore!

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:41.420
I got away from the village and achieved
my dream of starting a new life!

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:45.800
And after all that, I got dragged
right back to Hinamizawa!

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:49.090
Do you know what that means?!

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:53.430
That means that if I can use
this new power to escape again,

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:57.720
one day, out of nowhere,
I might be whisked away to 1983 again!

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:00.640
Do you know how horrifying that is?!

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:02.150
I'm sorry.

00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:07.940
If you disappear,
then I'll really, truly be alone!

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:19.370
Rika, I didn't want to have
to tell you about this...

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:23.040
But now, it shall be my parting words.

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:24.250
Huh?

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:27.130
Of the many artifacts bearing my name,

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:32.760
the most important, most holy
of them is a sacred sword,

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:35.510
Onigari-no-ryuou.

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:39.520
It has the ability to kill those for whom
death is no end, but beginning:

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:42.480
it can kill one who lives in loops.

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:45.310
A sword that can kill
one who lives in loops?

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:48.820
But you are no longer a fledgling.

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:50.150
Wait!

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:52.360
Goodbye, Rika.

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:57.080
Your life and future must be
shaped by your own hands.

00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:00.370
Wait! Don't go, Hanyuu!

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:02.910
Hanyuu!

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:09.710
I hope you'll have a cream puff
for me every now and then.

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:10.630
No!

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:14.970
I only made it through those hundred years
because you were there with me!

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:19.180
If you leave me, if you're gone--!

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:26.060
I can't do this! Not without you!

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:29.940
I want to play hide-and-seek.

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:32.860
Hide-and-seek? Huh, that's random.

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.780
I like hide-and-seek!

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:38.660
Where are we allowed to hide?
Anywhere on school grounds?

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:41.410
That's too small!
We'll be found too quickly!

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:44.710
Anywhere in Hinamizawa is okay.

00:10:44.710 --> 00:10:48.040
Anywhere in the village?
That's a big area.

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:53.720
I'll use my crafty trapmaking skills to
ensnare and deter anyone looking for me!

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:57.470
Satoko, the only person
hiding is going to be me.

00:10:58.180 --> 00:10:59.470
Just you?

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:04.060
Rika! You must be around here, I know it!

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:07.600
Just give yourself up already, now!

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:33.710
Now that I recall, I came here while
playing hide-and-seek once before.

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:39.090
I hid inside the ritual tool shed, and
when Rika was blamed for my mistake,

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:41.100
she was punished.

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:44.220
It wasn't me! It wasn't me!

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:46.060
I'm sorry!

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:51.570
How long ago was that?
How many centuries ago?

00:11:51.570 --> 00:11:54.230
I can't remember anymore.

00:12:32.440 --> 00:12:37.320
I'd better keep this dangerous
weapon far away from Rika.

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:52.460
Silly Hanyuu. It's not here.

00:12:52.460 --> 00:12:55.210
There's no sword!

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:57.510
You left me this parting gift
I didn't even want,

00:12:57.510 --> 00:12:59.760
and it's not even here!

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:21.400
Mion! Your hunch says
she's gonna be at the shrine?

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:27.120
It's Rika-<i>chan</i>'s home, so she must
know lots of places to hide there.

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:31.290
It's my home, too,
and I've looked all over for her.

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:33.960
If Rika-<i>chan </i>were really trying
to keep us from finding her,

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:36.000
then she'd be here.

00:13:49.310 --> 00:13:50.640
Rika-<i>chan</i>!

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:54.350
Rika! Come out if you're in there!

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:57.650
Rika-<i>chan</i>! Please come out!

00:13:57.650 --> 00:14:01.700
We might've lost today,
but we won't let you win tomorrow!

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:08.330
I can die whenever I want now.

00:14:08.330 --> 00:14:13.080
Rika, you know no matter where
you hide, I'll always find you!

00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:18.670
Five more loops.

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:20.380
I'll try for five more loops,

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:22.760
and if I don't succeed...

00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:25.930
...I'll give up.

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:29.600
After all, I certainly can't
let you get away from me.

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:32.970
Wednesday

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:32.970
June

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:39.860
Akasaka-<i>san</i>, if I'm correct?

00:14:39.860 --> 00:14:42.900
Yes, that's me, Mamoru Akasaka.

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:45.490
Wait, were you at that
toy store in Okinomiya?

00:14:45.490 --> 00:14:47.320
Yes, I'm Satoko Hojo.

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:52.080
You seem to be well-acquainted with Rika,
though I'm not sure of the reason.

00:14:52.080 --> 00:14:55.040
Well, I owe her my life.

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:59.460
So whatever she needs, I'm there for her.

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:06.970
In that case, I need to tell you
the real reason why Rika is suffering.

00:15:06.970 --> 00:15:08.300
The <i>real </i>reason?

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:12.470
Most people wouldn't
believe me if they tried.

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:14.390
You see...

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:19.610
She's infected with parasites
that have taken control of her.

00:15:19.610 --> 00:15:21.570
I'm sure I can do something to help.

00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:28.320
You don't need to
worry anymore, Rika-<i>chan</i>!

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:32.040
Now all the parasites
inside of you are gone!

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:34.540
I <i>saved </i>you, Rika-<i>chan</i>!

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:38.540
Right.

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:41.630
Itchy, itchy, itchy, itchy!

00:15:41.630 --> 00:15:44.010
I know how to kill you, you damn bugs!

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:50.800
Itchy, itchy, itchy, itchy!

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:55.430
You filthy parasites!
I'll burn you all to a fucking crisp!

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:02.440
Rika! Rika!

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:05.030
Shout if you're all right!

00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:06.990
Rika!

00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:08.410
Rika-<i>chan</i>!

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:10.780
No!

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:13.030
Call the fire department! Hurry!

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:14.870
C'mon, now!

00:16:14.870 --> 00:16:18.370
Rika, I do hope you
realize sooner than later...

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:22.290
...that this is the curse.

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:27.720
Oyashiro-<i>sama</i>'s curse.

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:42.860
This is the worst... My neck is so itchy!

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:45.190
Itchy, itchy, itchy...

00:16:47.990 --> 00:16:52.120
It must be unbearably itchy for you, too.

00:16:54.370 --> 00:16:56.120
It is.

00:16:56.120 --> 00:17:00.870
Though thanks to you, I can't
move my arms to scratch my neck.

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:06.210
I'm truly sorry you had to
be born into the Furude family.

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:13.220
If fate was mine to choose, I would have
never wanted to be born in Hinamizawa!

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:14.550
I agree.

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:20.100
We fell victim to Hinamizawa's
curse the moment we were born.

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:21.520
It hurts, doesn't it?

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:24.480
It's so painful and itchy, isn't it?

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:26.820
It's okay.

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:29.650
I'll make you feel all better!

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:31.860
Yes, please do.

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:35.700
Put an end to this so I can
move on to the next world.

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:39.330
I'll be right behind you,

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:43.250
just as soon as I destroy
your Hinamizawa blood!

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:48.130
Who's there?

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:52.340
Is that you, Satoko-<i>chan</i>?

00:17:53.760 --> 00:18:00.310
How odd. You look just like Satoko-<i>chan</i>,
but you surely aren't her.

00:18:00.310 --> 00:18:03.520
Have you taken care of my dear Rika?

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:06.230
Whyever do you ask?

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:08.940
It's extremely important that I know.

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:11.110
Oh.

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:16.370
Seems I needn't worry after all.

00:18:24.250 --> 00:18:27.630
I see. There <i>was </i>a demon in our midst.

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:34.970
I'm not a <i>demon</i>.

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:44.810
You know good and well that
when Oyashiro-<i>sama </i>gets mad,

00:18:44.810 --> 00:18:50.150
the good women of the Furude family must
be sacrificed to quell his wrath, yes?

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:53.150
...shut up.

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:59.580
You must be happy to be followin' in
your ancestors' footsteps, miss Rika.

00:18:59.580 --> 00:19:01.660
Just shut up.

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:05.080
How can they still not get it?!

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:07.750
Oryo-<i>san</i>'s completely useless!

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:09.630
Same with Mion-<i>chan</i>!

00:19:09.630 --> 00:19:12.880
No one understands their
responsibility to this village!

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:14.930
Damn whippersnappers...

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:20.060
Kimiyoshi, could you finish your monologue
<i>after </i>tossing me in the swamp?

00:19:20.060 --> 00:19:25.190
My, my, you sure understand the roles
and responsibilities our families play!

00:19:25.190 --> 00:19:28.400
No, your breath just stinks.

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:30.730
How dare you talk back to your elders?!

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:33.530
You rude little wretch!

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:55.260
Oyashiro-<i>sama</i>, Oyashiro-<i>sama</i>!
Please, be angry no more!

00:19:55.260 --> 00:19:59.220
Let this have quelled your rage!
Please, forgive us!

00:19:59.220 --> 00:20:02.470
If she can hold her breath this long,

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:06.020
then she'll have doubled the world record.

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:18.610
Now things are <i>really </i>getting fun, Rena!

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:23.620
How can you say that, Keiichi-<i>kun</i>?!
This isn't fun at all!

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:27.460
Well, <i>I've </i>been having a ton of fun!

00:20:27.460 --> 00:20:34.090
But I bet it'll be even <i>more </i>fun
when I split your head open!

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:41.050
It doesn't stop.

00:20:41.050 --> 00:20:44.560
Boy, fun like this
reminds me of club, doesn't it?!

00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:47.390
You're right, but look!

00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:49.980
Nobody wants to live in this world!

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:55.230
This is all just a bad dream!

00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:58.490
So please, wake up, Keiichi-<i>kun</i>!

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:08.660
It won't give me a place
or time to catch my breath.

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:20.180
Truly, there are no better
storytellers than the lot of you.

00:21:20.180 --> 00:21:23.680
I am quite satisfied, child of man.

00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:30.560
The story you are weaving
will surely cure me of my boredom!

00:21:40.280 --> 00:21:41.910
What's this?

00:22:00.550 --> 00:22:02.930
If it isn't my darling failure.

00:22:06.890 --> 00:22:09.560
At long last, I've found you!

00:23:41.980 --> 00:23:46.980
God-Entertaining Chapter, Part 2

00:23:43.130 --> 00:23:46.920
Next time: "Kagurashi-hen:
God-Entertaining Chapter, Part 2."
